# RNGFND1 override for the downward-facing Gazebo LiDAR, injected via MAVLink
# DISTANCE_SENSOR by lidar_bridge.py (see CLAUDE.md, Sensor Fusion Architecture).
#
# gazebo-iris.parm sets RNGFND1_TYPE=1 (Analog, fed by SIM_SONAR_SCALE) — the
# render-driven-only philosophy for this project means we do NOT use that
# path. Loaded as the last (most specific) file in sim_vehicle.py's --defaults
# list, so these values override gazebo-iris.parm's RNGFND1_* block.
#
# Values match the gpu_lidar sensor's <range> block in
# iris_with_standoffs/model.sdf (min 0.05 m, max 40 m).
RNGFND1_TYPE 10
RNGFND1_ORIENT 25
RNGFND1_MIN 0.05
RNGFND1_MAX 40
# Rangefinder body-frame position offset (FRD, +Z down). LiDAR at z=-0.12 m in
# the SDF; on centreline, X=Y=0. This is the true physical value.
#
# IMPORTANT: this does NOT affect the optical-flow scale error - it CANCELS out
# of the flow terrain-height path (see the FLOW_POS_Z note in flow_ekf.parm:
# pd cancels in heightAboveGnd = terrainState - pd, and readRangeFinder never
# applies this offset to the range anyway). It is set to the true 0.12 for the
# height-ESTIMATE path (EK3_SRC1_POSZ=2/RangeFinder), where it correctly refers
# the origin height to the ground datum. Setting it does no harm to flow and
# corrects a real geometry statement for the height source. See CLAUDE.md.
RNGFND1_POS_X 0
RNGFND1_POS_Y 0
RNGFND1_POS_Z 0.12
